<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paide</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Weissenstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paide, known in German as Weissenstein, is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Järva County</a>. It grew around a castle built by the Livonian Order in 1265, whose octagonal tower, the Vallitorn, has been rebuilt. The town was fought over in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a> and later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paide.jpg" alt="Paide" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ivo Kruusamägi · CC BY-SA 3.0 ee · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paide_ordulinnuse_varemed_2013.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
